The key labelled "delete" on a Mac sends Backspace, and only forward Delete (fn+delete) erased the selection, so the obvious key did nothing.

On macOS (native, and the web build via egui's user-agent detection), Backspace now erases selected objects, but only when it can't be meant for the command line:
- a fresh press, never an auto-repeat, so holding delete to clear typing can't run on into the drawing;
- a plain press: Option/Cmd+delete delete a word or line of text on macOS;
- no command running and the command line empty;
- nothing typed at the command line since the selection was made (typing, then clearing it, leaves delete editing text until the selection changes).

Windows and Linux are unchanged: Backspace only edits the command line there. The decision is a small pure function with unit tests.


