Part of #406.

## The problem

CADCraft had no AUDIT and no RECOVER (docs/gaps.md F4). A drawing with broken internals — objects on layers that don't exist, references to missing styles or block definitions, NaN coordinates, a block that contains itself, two objects with one handle — could not be checked or repaired, and a damaged file could only be opened as it was.

## Changes

- **`crates/engine/src/audit.rs`** (new): `audit::check(&Drawing)` reports, `audit::fix(&mut Drawing)` / `audit::repair` fix. Checks and fixes:
  - required table entries (layer 0, ByBlock/ByLayer/Continuous, the Standard text, dimension, multileader and table styles) → recreated with defaults;
  - layers with missing linetypes → Continuous; dimension and multileader styles with missing text styles → Standard;
  - current-entry variables (CLAYER, CELTYPE, TEXTSTYLE, DIMSTYLE, CMLEADERSTYLE, CTABLESTYLE) naming missing entries → `0` / `ByLayer` / `Standard`;
  - invalid geometry: NaN or infinite numbers (the serializer walk from `finite.rs`), zero-length lines, circles and arcs with radius ≤ 0, ellipses with no size → removed;
  - handle 0 and handles used twice (across model space, layouts and block definitions) → new handles; a handle seed not above the largest handle → moved past it;
  - block references to missing block definitions → an empty definition is created (the references and their attributes stay);
  - objects on missing layers → the layer is created; missing linetypes → ByLayer; missing text, dimension, multileader and table styles → Standard; a dimension's missing `*D` block → dropped (it draws itself again); dimension associations, group members and constraints that point at missing objects → dropped; viewport frozen-layer and VP colour lists naming missing layers → those entries dropped;
  - block definitions that contain themselves, directly or through others → the reference closing the loop is removed (iterative search, no recursion).
