Part of #451.

## The problem
Hatches were created with `associative: true`, but nothing tied them to their boundary: moving, stretching or scaling the boundary left the hatch behind, and the link wasn't saved to DXF (every loop was written with `97 0`).

## Changes
- **Model**: `HatchLoop::sources` (serde default, omitted when empty) holds the handles of the objects a loop was made from. Pick point: the curves along the traced face (new `Boundary::outer_sources` from the region tracer) and each island's curves; select objects: the object. Non-associative hatches keep none. `HPASSOC` sets the default of the `associative` parameter.
- **Following** (`cmd/hatch/assoc.rs`, called from the post-command pass in `assoc::after_command`, so it runs after `Session::execute` and after interactive commands):
  - only hatches whose own source objects changed are traced again (a scan of the hatches, then work proportional to the touched ones);
  - one closed object → its loop; several curves → the face around a point inside the old loop, carried along with the objects' extents (move, scale, stretch), falling back to the outline of the curves; islands → the outside outline of their curves;
  - an erased island → the loop goes and the hatch fills its area;
  - an erased outer boundary or one that no longer encloses an area → the hatch keeps its shape, becomes non-associative and a message says so;
  - the hatch moved or reshaped on its own → no longer associative;
  - a new hatch (COPY, paste, EXPLODE) whose loops aren't where its objects are → no longer associative (copies aren't re-linked to copied boundaries yet).
  - hostile input: at most 4096 sources per loop are traced, at most 1000 new hatches checked per command (the rest lose the link); hatches are never boundaries.
- **Geometry** (`geom::region`): `Boundary::outer_sources`, `outline()` (outside outline of curves that form one closed group) and `interior_point()`; the island tracer shares the new `outside()` helper.
