## The problem
The canvas had a single right-click menu. While a command ran, right-click could only mean Enter, so the prompt's options, recent input and snap overrides were out of reach from the mouse. A selection got the same generic items whatever was selected.

## Changes
- **Command menu, opened by holding the right button** (`context_menu::in_command`). This follows AutoCAD's time-sensitive right-click: a quick click is still Enter, and holding for 250 ms (`HOLD_SECS`) opens the menu at the pointer. It has:
  - Enter and Cancel;
  - Recent Input (values typed at prompts, newest first);
  - the current prompt's options (from `Session::current_prompt().keywords`);
  - Snap Overrides at point prompts (the object snap menu as a submenu);
  - Pan ▸ and Zoom ▸, typed transparently (`'zoom.extents`), so the command keeps running.

  Each item gives the command the same input as typing it.
- **Idle and selection menu**, extended:
  - Recent Commands;
  - Isolate ▸ and Draw Order ▸;
  - Group/Ungroup, Add Selected, Select Similar;
  - the edit commands for the selected object type when all selected objects share one type: Edit Text, Block Editor/Edit Attributes, Hatch Edit, Polyline Edit, Spline Edit, Dimension Text Edit, plus Multileader, Viewport and Image edits once those commands exist;
  - Options.

  Items are built from command ids and appear only if the command is registered, so ISOLATEOBJECTS/SELECTSIMILAR (#434), DRAWORDER above/under (#446) and similar commands show up once they merge. No items are stubbed.
- Engine: a read-only `Session::recent_commands(max)` built from the command log (new `crates/engine/src/recent.rs`).
- `canvas.rs` changes one line: the Enter-on-right-click condition now asks `context_menu::in_command`. The grip-menu code in #440 is untouched.
- Ukrainian translations for the new labels.

