## The problem
Right-clicking the command line, the drawing tabs, the layout tabs or the palettes did nothing (the Layers palette rows had no menu; only the Layer Properties Manager dialog did).

## Changes
New `crates/ui-egui/src/shortcut_menus.rs`. Menus are built from command ids and act through `app.run` / `app.start` / the running command's prompts. Items for commands that aren't registered are left out.

- **Command line:**
  - Recent Commands;
  - Dynamic Input;
  - Command History (F2) and Lines of Command History ▸;
  - Copy History (the log to the system clipboard);
  - Clear Command History (new UI command `ui.cmdline.clear`).
- **Drawing tabs:**
  - New, Open;
  - Save and Save As, which act on the right-clicked drawing;
  - Close, Close All Other Drawings (new `CadApp::request_close_others`, so "Save changes?" is asked as usual);
  - Copy Full File Path.
- **Layout tabs:**
  - New Layout;
  - From Template, Delete Layout, Rename Layout and Copy Layout, all through LAYOUT's own prompts, so Rename and Copy ask for the new name on the command line;
  - Page Setup Manager and Print for the right-clicked layout.
  - The Model tab offers only New Layout and From Template.
- **Layers palette rows:** Set Current, Turn Off/On, Freeze/Thaw, Lock/Unlock, Delete Layer, Layer Properties Manager.
- **Properties palette background:** Quick Select, Select All, Deselect All, Hide Palette.
- Hooks are one or two lines each in `cmdline.rs`, `chrome.rs` (the tab closure now also returns its response), `palettes.rs` and `docking.rs`.
- Ukrainian translations for the new labels. `docs/ui-parity.md` is updated.

