Part of #563.

## The problem
CAL was a number-only evaluator and QUICKCALC/QC were just aliases of it: there was no QuickCalc palette, no unit conversion, no variables or history, and no way to read coordinates, distances, angles or intersections from the drawing into a calculation (`docs/gaps.md` F22).

## Changes
- **CAL evaluator** (`crates/engine/src/cmd/utility/calc.rs`, moved out of `utility.rs`):
  - points `[x,y]` (a Z is accepted and ignored) and polar `[d<a]`; vector `+ -`, scaling, `*` dot product, `&` cross product;
  - vector and point functions: `dist`, `ang` (vector, line, or angle at an apex), `vec`, `vec1`, `ill`, `plt`, `pld`, `rot`, `abs` of a vector; n-ary `min`/`max`; `exp10`; exponents with a sign (`1e-3`);
  - variables may be numbers or points (case-insensitive);
  - same caps as before (length, nesting depth) plus an argument cap; `eval` keeps its number-only signature.
- **CAL JSON**: `{expr}` → `{value}` or `{point}`; `{convert: {type?, from, to, value}}` converts length, area, volume and angle units (results rounded to 14 significant digits so 2 ft is 24 in); `{units: true}` lists the unit tables; `{pick, points}` reads a value from points. Typed `CAL` now asks `>> Expression:` and echoes the value.
- **QUICKCALC.PICK**: `Get from the drawing or [Point/Distance/Angle/Intersection]:`, then the point prompts (snaps, typed coordinates), then echoes `QuickCalc: <value>`. The JSON form takes `{mode, points}`.
- **QuickCalc palette** (`crates/ui-egui/src/palettes/quickcalc.rs`), opened by typing QUICKCALC/QC, Window > QuickCalc or Cmd+8 (with JSON parameters `quickcalc` still runs CAL):
  - a dock panel (`quickCalc`) outside the default arrangement that floats by the right edge of the drawing the first time and comes back where it was closed;
  - expression field (Enter or `=`), history (click to reuse an expression or its result), `ans`, Clear, Paste to Command Line;
