## The problem
There was no way to compare two drawings (`docs/gaps.md` F22): no list of what was added, removed or changed, no overlay, and no way to step through the differences.

## Changes
- **COMPARE** (`crates/engine/src/cmd/file/compare.rs`) compares the tab shown with the same space of another drawing:
  - the other drawing is a file read through the io hooks (`{path}`, or `{data, name}` as OPEN takes it) or an open drawing (`{document: index or title}`). On the web, where there are no paths, the error says to open the drawing and compare with it by name;
  - matching: (1) the same handle with equal geometry and properties; (2) equal geometry and properties under another handle, so files written by other programs still match; (3) the same handle and type with other geometry or properties is a **change**, reported as geometry, properties or both. What is left is only in this drawing or only in the other one;
  - geometry is a hash of the object's rounded JSON. A block reference also hashes its definition's contents (memoised, bounded by `MAX_BLOCK_DEPTH` and a work cap). What a dimension derives from its geometry (its generated block, its cached measurement, a text position the user didn't set) is ignored, so a drawing written to DXF and read back compares as unchanged;
  - capped at 200,000 objects per drawing (`truncated` says so), with at most 1,000 listed per kind of difference;
  - change areas: the differences are bucketed on a 32 × 32 grid over their extents, in reading order;
  - JSON: `{other, added, removed, changed: [{handle, other, type, what}], counts, regions, truncated, message}`.
  - At the command line: `Enter the drawing to compare with (an open drawing's name or a file path):`.
